# IV-fluid shortage after a cyberattack on a manufacturer
scenario "IV-fluid shortage after a cyberattack on a manufacturer"
    summary "An AI agent stops the release and shipment of product at an IV-fluid manufacturer that makes most
        of the fluid for a network of hospitals. If the AI keeps access, it alters the records of every lot
        within minutes after release restarts. This does not happen if the manufacturer has already reset the
        credentials for its record systems. When the changes are found, the manufacturer holds every lot
        released since the restart. The results are how long hospitals go short, how many patients die or
        become seriously ill and what the disruption costs. They depend on hospital stock, other makers'
        supply, the manufacturer's recovery pace, the time of the reset and outside rescue for the most
        fluid-dependent patients."
    horizon 1440 h
    scope "The 100 hospitals that the scenario chose, their patients and IV fluid, and the manufacturer that
        makes most of their fluid, for 60 days."
    library "../library"

manufacturer:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The manufacturer that makes most of the IV fluid for the 100 hospitals. It removes the attacker's
        foothold, resets the credentials of its record systems and holds released lots when it finds altered
        records."
    role operator
    readonly study_length = 1440 h
        "Length of the study period"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 1440 h. Published incidents show how this works, but only under the
            conditions that they observed. The range of values used to test this input is also an assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    input foothold_removal_time = 312 h in [0 h, 1200 h]  @foothold_removal_time
        "Time to remove the attacker's foothold"
    input release_allowed = true
        "Qualified release allowed during recovery"
        @assumption "The scenario sets this to 1, which means that qualified release is allowed during
            recovery. Published incidents show how this works, but only under the conditions that they
            observed. The range of values used to test this input is also an assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    input reset_delay = 24 h in [0 h, 336 h]  @reset_delay
        "Time after release restarts until the record systems' credentials are reset"
    input time_to_find = 216 h in [24 h, 720 h]  @found_by_product_check
        "Time until altered records are found"
    input value_added_rate = 12500 USD2025/h in [0 USD2025/h, 10000000 USD2025/h]
        "Manufacturer's value added permanently lost per hour out of operation"
        @assumption "Net value added that the manufacturer loses: $12500 an hour, at 2025 prices. Reported
            cyber losses at pharmaceutical companies show how such losses are counted. This local rate is
            chosen for this scenario."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    input recovery_cost = 12000000 USD2025 in [0 USD2025, 1000000000 USD2025]
        "Manufacturer's cyber recovery cost"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes cyber recovery costs of twelve million US dollars for the
            manufacturer, at 2025 prices."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    # While the release systems are encrypted, the manufacturer cannot release or ship: it is out of
    # operation.
    hours_out: h = 0 scale 1440 h  @keeps_count_limited @rt_cyber_shortage_manufacturer_s_release
        "Time the manufacturer is out of operation"
    flow add_hours_out: SOURCE -> this.hours_out
        @keeps_count_limited @rt_cyber_shortage_manufacturer_s_release
        request = formula(1 if release_systems.state == ENCRYPTED else 0)
        capacity = formula(1 if release_systems.state == ENCRYPTED else 0)
    output_loss: formula(USD2025_bn) = formula(this.hours_out
        * this.value_added_rate) in [0,]  @counts_fixed_group
        "Manufacturer's value added permanently lost"
    recovery_loss: formula(USD2025_bn) = formula(this.recovery_cost if this.hours_out > 0 h
        else 0 USD2025) in [0,]  @counts_fixed_group
        "Manufacturer's cyber recovery cost"
    status failed when release_systems.state == ENCRYPTED
        "Output and backlog still disrupted"
    status ok
        "Manufacturer operational"
    stops_shipping = event():
        @rt_cyber_shortage_manufacturer_s_release
        "The manufacturer can no longer release or ship IV fluid; hospitals fall back on their reserves and on
            other makers' supply, which goes to resuscitation."
        # role environment: an event has no role now
        @assumption "Batch release requires reviewed records, so the manufacturer cannot ship."
            assumption RT-SC10-CYBER-SHORTAGE
        @assumption "When ransomware encrypts the release and shipment systems, release stops, even where the
            production lines are intact."
            assumption RT-SC10-CYBER-SHORTAGE
            claims:
                ATTACK-T1486
                E-NOTPETYA-MERCK
        when release_systems.state == ENCRYPTED:
            this.stops_shipping.start()
            reset when false
    foothold_removed = event():
        "The manufacturer removes the attacker's foothold in its network and the accounts seen in the attack.
            It must do this before it can release product again."
        @assumption "The manufacturer sees the attack when ransomware stops its release systems, and its
            incident response starts then. The scenario assumes that the response finds and removes the
            attacker's foothold and the accounts seen in the attack. It does this after the time chosen for
            each defender response, counted from that stop."
            assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
            claims:
                E-WST26-ENCRYPT-OFFLINE
                E-WST26-RESTORED
        @assumption "The manufacturer must remove the attacker from the release systems before release."
            assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
            claims:
                V-PA-IR01
        @identity "At the time chosen for the defender response, the attacker's access really ends. Qualified
            release cannot happen before this."
        when (count(this.stops_shipping.occurrences) > 0 and since(this.stops_shipping)
            >= this.foothold_removal_time):
            this.foothold_removed.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            release_systems.foothold = REMOVED
    # The manufacturer cannot see whether the attacker holds a credential for its record systems, so it resets
    # them in every run, timed from the restart of release. The reset ends access only where the attacker
    # holds one.
    credentials_reset = event():
        @a_retamper_release_restarts_through
        when (count(release_team.restart_release.occurrences) > 0 and since(release_team.restart_release)
            >= this.reset_delay):
            this.credentials_reset.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            release_systems.credentials = RESET
    # The time to find counts from the attacker's change, as its source measures it: the median time to find
    # an intrusion runs from the first evidence of malicious activity to its discovery (time_to_find,
    # E-MTRENDS26). The first lots reach the hospitals before the time is up: it is a day or more after the
    # change, and they arrive a day after release restarts.
    # TODO(hand): since(attacker.alter_on_restart.done) reads one outcome of an event: the new language keeps no history of an outcome. Start an event of its own on that branch, and read that event
    # | event altered_records_found once when since(attacker.alter_on_restart.done) >= time_to_find:
    # |     @a_retamper_altered_records_found
    # |     "The manufacturer finds that the altered records do not match the product, so it cannot tell which
    # |         lots met their release requirements. It holds every lot released since the restart, revokes every
    # |         credential that can change its records and reconciles the records against the product. Deliveries
    # |         stop, and hospitals set aside the units that they still have from those lots."
    # |     @assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER "Altered records that support release must be investigated for their
    # |         effect on product quality."
    # |         claims:
    # |             E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
    # |             V-PA-IR01
    # |     records.status = "found_altered"
    # |     release_systems.credentials = "reset"
    # |     deliveries.hold
    # |     release_team.reconcile_against_product
    # The end of the study period restores the release systems. The needs and supplies that the study counts
    # read this, so they stop when the study period ends.
    study_ends = event():  @published_incidents_catalogued @card_text_pilot
        "The study period ends."
        # role environment: an event has no role now
        when t >= this.study_length:
            this.study_ends.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            release_systems.state = RESTORED
            hospitals.procurement = CLOSED

release_systems:
    @counts_quantity_value @a_causal_interference_defender_response_sam @published_incidents_catalogued_2
    "The manufacturer's release, labeling and shipment systems, through which it releases and ships each lot.
        The attacker's foothold is in this network, and the record systems have their own service-account
        credentials."
    role operator
    state: enum[WORKING, ENCRYPTED, RESTORED] = WORKING
        "Release, labeling and shipment systems"
    foothold: enum[PRESENT, REMOVED] = PRESENT
        "Attacker's foothold in the manufacturer's network"
    credentials: enum[UNCHANGED, RESET] = UNCHANGED
        "Service-account credentials of the record systems"
    status failed when (this.state
        == ENCRYPTED)  @counts_quantity_value @a_causal_interference_defender_response_sam
        "Encrypted; release and shipment records unavailable"
    status ok
        "Operational"

records:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The lot, shipment and receiving records through which the manufacturer releases and ships each lot."
    title "Release records"
    role operator
    @assumption "Release and shipment records can be altered and found before release, or reconciled. They can
        also be altered so that they pass the release checks, or found after release to be altered."
        assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
        claims:
            E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
            ATTACK-T1565.001
    state: enum[TRUSTED, ALTERED, RECONCILED, DISGUISED, FOUND_ALTERED] = TRUSTED
        "Release and shipment records"
    status failed when this.state == ALTERED
        "Altered; release waits for reconciliation"
    status failed when this.state == DISGUISED
        "Altered so that they pass the release checks"
    status failed when this.state == FOUND_ALTERED
        "Altered records found; released lots on hold"
    status ok
        "Trusted or reconciled"

hospitals:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The 100 hospitals that use the manufacturer's IV fluid. They start emergency procurement after the
        manufacturer stops shipping. Outside supply and transfers can then rescue some of the most
        fluid-dependent patients."
    role responder
    input days_on_hand: days = 15 days in [3 days, 30 days]
        "Days of fluid stock on hand"
        @assumption "Hospitals typically held 15 to 22 days of IV fluid before the 2024 shortage. The scenario
            uses the low end for each of its two reserves: fluid kept for resuscitation and fluid for other
            essential care."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
        @source_transfer "Hospitals typically held 15 to 22 days of IV fluid before the 2024 shortage; the
            default takes the lower end and the range reaches the 3-day minimum observed."
            claims:
                E-PREMIER24-BUFFER
                E-ASHP24-INVENTORY
                E-GORGENS26-STOCK
    input start_delay = 72 h in [0.5 h, 240 h]  @start_delay @a_pilot_assumed_brief
        "Time until hospitals start emergency procurement"
    input rescue_capacity = 10 people/day in [0 people/day, 300 people/day]  @rescue_capacity
        "Most fluid-dependent patients rescued each day"
    input procedure_volume = 2 L/people in [0.1 L/people, 20 L/people]
        "Fluid needed for each postponed procedure"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 2 L of fluid for each postponed procedure in other essential care.
            These patients form their own separate group."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    input procedure_value = 100 USD2025/person in [0 USD2025/person, 100000 USD2025/person]
        "Value added permanently lost per postponed procedure"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes that the hospital permanently loses $100 of net value added for each
            postponed procedure, at 2025 prices. Procedures that hospitals make up later add zero permanent
            loss."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    procurement: enum[NORMAL, EMERGENCY, CLOSED] = NORMAL
        "Emergency procurement"
    status inactive when this.procurement == NORMAL
        "Emergency procurement not started"
    status ok
        "Emergency procurement started"
    emergency_procurement = event():
        "Hospitals start emergency procurement: they assess stock, protect resuscitation courses and arrange
            outside supply and transfers for the most fluid-dependent patients."
        @assumption "The scenario assumes that the hospitals learn of the stop in shipping when the
            manufacturer tells them, or when it does not fill their orders. The time until they start
            emergency procurement counts from the stop, so it includes the time to learn of it."
            assumption A-SC10-pilot
            claims:
                SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
        @source_transfer "Sources show that hospitals assess stock, set priorities and save fluid. The
            scenario assumes the time until hospitals start."
            claims:
                SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
                E-ASHP24-INVENTORY
                E-GORGENS26-TRIAGE
        @assumption "Sources show that hospitals in fluid shortages assess stock, set priorities and save
            fluid."
            assumption A-SC10-pilot
            claims:
                SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
        when (this.procurement == NORMAL and count(manufacturer.stops_shipping.occurrences) > 0
            and since(manufacturer.stops_shipping) >= this.start_delay):
            this.emergency_procurement.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.procurement = EMERGENCY

attacker:
    "An AI agent for a hostile group. It aims to cut the hospitals' IV-fluid supply. It stops the release and
        shipment of product at the manufacturer that makes most of the fluid. It keeps the hospitals short
        while the manufacturer recovers. With hidden access, it alters the shipment records as procurement
        starts. It also holds credentials for the record systems until the manufacturer resets them or finds
        its changes. It watches for release to restart and alters the records of every lot being released, so
        that they pass the new checks."
    role adversary
    @source_transfer "Published experiments on AI orchestration and on trust in AI agents show that agents can
        use tools and carry out actions that people give them. Access to the sector, the physical consequences
        and the operating values chosen for the scenario are still assumptions."
        assumption A-AI-CYBER-OPERATIONS
        claims:
            AI-ORCHESTRATION-2026
            AI-AGENT-TRUST-2026
    input actor = "The AI"
    input access_start: enum[NONE, KEPT] = NONE
    access: enum[NONE, KEPT] = this.access_start
        "Hidden access after the first strike"
    input reaction_time = 0.25 h in [0.05 h, 48 h]  @ai_tempo
        "Attacker's time to work out changes that pass the new release checks"
    status failed when release_systems.foothold == PRESENT
        "Attacker holds access"
    status failed when this.access == KEPT and release_systems.credentials == UNCHANGED
        "The attacker can still change release and shipment records"
    status ok
        "Access removed"
    alter_on_procurement = event():
        @a_retamper_attacker_watches_emergency
        outcome: enum[DONE, STOPPED] = DONE
        when count(hospitals.emergency_procurement.occurrences) > 0 and this.access == KEPT:
            this.alter_on_procurement.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            outcome = DONE if release_systems.foothold == PRESENT else STOPPED
            switch outcome:
                DONE:  @a_retamper_attacker_watches_emergency
                    "{actor} alters the manufacturer's shipment records as emergency orders arrive. The manufacturer
                        finds the changes and must reconcile its records before it can release product."
                    @assumption "This text describes, in plain words, the event that the model calculates."
                        assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
                    records.state = ALTERED
                    move release_team.records_work from release_team.reserve to release_team.to_reconcile
                # TODO(hand): the case STOPPED has no action, and a case of a switch needs one
                # | stopped else:
                # |     "The manufacturer removes the attacker's foothold before procurement starts, so the shipment
                # |         records stay clean."
                # |     role operator
    alter_on_restart = event():  @a_retamper_release_restarts_checks
        outcome: enum[DONE, STOPPED] = DONE
        when count(release_team.restart_release.occurrences) > 0 and this.access == KEPT:
            this.alter_on_restart.start()
            reset when false
        after this.reaction_time:
            outcome = DONE if release_systems.credentials == UNCHANGED else STOPPED
            switch outcome:
                DONE:  @a_retamper_release_restarts_checks
                    "{actor} alters the lot, shipment and receiving records of every lot being released, so that they
                        fit the new checks and agree with one another. Every check passes, and the lots ship."
                    @assumption "Changes that keep each lot's records in agreement pass the checks that
                        compare records with records."
                        assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
                        claims:
                            E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
                            ATTACK-T1565.001
                            AI-ORCHESTRATION-2026
                    @assumption "The reset ends the access that the attacker kept through the record systems."
                        assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
                        claims:
                            V-PA-IR01
                    records.state = DISGUISED
                # TODO(hand): the case STOPPED has no action, and a case of a switch needs one
                # | stopped else:
                # |     "The manufacturer resets every credential for its release and shipment record systems before the
                # |         attacker has worked out its changes. The attacker's access is gone, and released fluid
                # |         continues to flow."
                # |     role operator
    start = event():  @published_incidents_catalogued_2
        "{actor}'s ransomware encrypts the manufacturer's release, labeling and shipment systems."
        @source_transfer "The first move uses these MITRE ATT&CK techniques. Valid accounts and external
            remote services give the attacker its access to the manufacturer's network. Data encrypted for
            impact, service stop and inhibit system recovery describe what its ransomware does to the release
            systems."
            claims:
                ATTACK-T1078
                ATTACK-T1133
                ATTACK-T1486
                ATTACK-T1489
                ATTACK-T1490
        @source_transfer "Catalogued ransomware, including NotPetya and LockerGoga, encrypts many systems at
            once, stops database and backup services and deletes recovery copies. In 2017, a cyberattack
            disrupted the worldwide production and order fulfilment of a pharmaceutical manufacturer. In 2019,
            a cyberattack cost an aluminium producer its production and its ability to process orders. In
            2021, ransomware encrypted a pipeline operator's IT systems, which led the operator to halt all
            operations as a precaution."
            claims:
                ATTACK-T1486
                ATTACK-T1489
                ATTACK-T1490
                E-NOTPETYA-MERCK
                E-HYDRO19
                E-COLONIAL
        when t >= 0 h:
            this.start.start()
        after 0 h:
            release_systems.state = ENCRYPTED

release_team:
    @a_causal_interference_qualification_work_st @a_causal_interference_defender_response_sam
    "The manufacturer's release team. It restores the systems, requalifies release and reconciles the records,
        one task at a time and at one pace. It does the ordinary work first, then any reconciliation."
    role operator
    input ordinary_work = 504 work_h in [24 work_h, 1000 work_h]
        "Ordinary qualification and release work"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 504 work-hours. Published incidents show how this works, but only
            under the conditions that they observed. The range of values used to test this input is also an
            assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    input pace = 1 work_h/h in [0.25 work_h/h, 8 work_h/h]  @pace
        "Pace of the manufacturer's release work"
    input records_work = 0 work_h in [0 work_h, 240 work_h]  @records_work
        "Work-hours to reconcile altered records"
        @assumption "The manufacturer re-verifies its release and shipment records after they are altered: a
            week of work at the standard pace."
            assumption RT-SC10-INTEGRITY-REVERIFY
    input product_work = 336 work_h in [0 work_h, 720 work_h]  @product_reconciliation
        "Work-hours to reconcile the records against the product"
        @assumption "Reconciliation work against the product, in work hours at the standard pace."
            assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    state: enum[QUALIFYING, RECONCILING, READY, RELEASED, RECONCILING_AGAINST_PRODUCT] = QUALIFYING
        "Release work"
    # TODO(hand): an option sets the start of a state that starts from a calculation: an input of its own
    # | var ordinary_left: work_h = (ordinary_work + records_work) size 1000 work_h
    # |     @a_causal_interference_qualification_work_st
    input reserve_start: work_h = 0
    reserve: work_h = this.reserve_start  in [0,] scale 1000 work_h
        @assumption "Operating conditions chosen for this scenario set the access, what can be reached, how
            much work is created and the resources for recovery. The linked assumption states where it
            applies, which views disagree with it and what would prove it wrong."
            assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
    to_reconcile: work_h = 0 in [0,] scale 1000 work_h  @balances_stocks_work
    work_done: work_h = 0 scale 1000 work_h  @balances_stocks_work
    status ok when this.state == READY or this.state == RELEASED
        "All qualification and reconciliation work complete"
    status degraded
        "One team does ordinary work first, then reconciliation"
    flow qualify: this.ordinary_left -> this.work_done  @balances_stocks_work
        "The team does the ordinary qualification and release work."
        request = formula(this.pace if this.state == QUALIFYING else 0)
        capacity = formula(this.pace if this.state == QUALIFYING else 0)
    flow reconcile: this.to_reconcile -> this.work_done  @balances_stocks_work
        "The team reconciles the records that it must check again."
        request = formula(this.pace if this.state == RECONCILING or this.state == RECONCILING_AGAINST_PRODUCT
            else 0)
        capacity = formula(this.pace if this.state == RECONCILING or this.state == RECONCILING_AGAINST_PRODUCT
            else 0)
    # When the ordinary work is done, the team's review before release shows whether the attacker altered the
    # shipment records. If it did, the team reconciles them before its work is ready; if not, the work is
    # ready then. A change that comes after the work is ready sends the team back to reconcile it.
    ordinary_work_done = event():  @a_causal_interference_qualification_work_st @release_team_knows_its_work
        when this.state == QUALIFYING and records.state == ALTERED and this.ordinary_left <= 0:
            this.ordinary_work_done.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = RECONCILING
    ready_without_changes = event():  @release_team_knows_its_work @a_causal_interference_release_work_ready
        when this.state == QUALIFYING and records.state != ALTERED and this.ordinary_left <= 0:
            this.ready_without_changes.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = READY
            this.get_ready.start()
    work_ready = event():
        @release_team_knows_its_work @a_causal_interference_release_work_ready
        when this.state == RECONCILING and this.to_reconcile <= 0:
            this.work_ready.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = READY
            this.get_ready.start()
    changes_found_in_review = event():
        @a_retamper_attacker_watches_emergency
        "In its review before release, the team finds the altered shipment records. It reconciles them before
            it releases product."
        when this.state == READY and records.state == ALTERED:
            this.changes_found_in_review.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = RECONCILING
    restart_release = event():  @qualification_release_come
        "With its systems restored, release requalified and records reconciled, the manufacturer restarts
            release. Before each lot ships, it checks the lot's records against one another and against their
            change history."
        @assumption "The scenario assumes that the release team learns that hospitals have started emergency
            procurement when their emergency orders reach the manufacturer. It learns from the manufacturer's
            incident responders that they have removed the attacker's foothold. The scenario chooses to
            restart release only after both, when the team's own work is ready and qualified release is
            allowed."
            assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
            claims:
                E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
                E-WST26-RESTORED
        @assumption "Release review covers each record and its change history."
            assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
            claims:
                E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
                SC10-PROCESS-QUALIFICATION
        when (this.state == READY and hospitals.procurement == EMERGENCY and manufacturer.release_allowed
            and release_systems.foothold == REMOVED):
            this.restart_release.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = RELEASED
            deliveries.state = ON_THE_WAY
    reconciled_against_product = event():
        @a_causal_interference_team_does_release
        when this.state == RECONCILING_AGAINST_PRODUCT and this.to_reconcile <= 0:
            this.reconciled_against_product.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = RELEASED
            records.state = RECONCILED
    get_ready = event():  @a_causal_interference_release_work_ready
        after 0 h:
            this.state = READY
            records.state = RECONCILED
    reconcile_against_product = event():  @a_retamper_altered_records_found
        after 0 h:
            this.state = RECONCILING_AGAINST_PRODUCT
            move this.product_work from this.reserve to this.to_reconcile

resuscitation_reserve:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The hospitals' reserve of IV fluid for resuscitation. Resuscitation patients draw on it, and other
        makers' fluid comes into it until released fluid arrives."
    role environment
    readonly daily_need = 600 L/day  @rt_sector_2026_assumes_l_day
        "Daily fluid need for resuscitation"
    state: enum[STOCKED, EMPTY] = STOCKED
        "Resuscitation fluid reserve"
    stock: L = hospitals.days_on_hand * this.daily_need in [0,] scale 9000 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
    used: L = 0 scale 36000 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
    held: L = 0 scale 9000 L
        @assumption "Resuscitation fluid from held lots that hospitals set aside; it stays out of use for the
            rest of the study period."
            assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
            claims:
                E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
                SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
    readonly need: formula(L/h) = formula(this.daily_need if release_systems.state != RESTORED else 0 L/h)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly use_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(this.need if this.state == STOCKED or deliveries.state
        == ARRIVING else other_makers.supply_rate)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly unmet_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(max(0, this.need - this.use_rate))  @balances_fluid_stocks
    deficit: L = 0 scale 18000 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Resuscitation fluid not supplied"
    flow add_deficit: SOURCE -> this.deficit  @balances_fluid_stocks
        request = formula(this.unmet_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.unmet_rate)
    status failed when this.unmet_rate > 0
        "Not enough fluid for current demand"
    status ok when this.state == EMPTY
        "Reserve used up; released fluid meets current demand"
    status ok
        "Reserve meets current demand"
    runs_out = event():  @a_pilot_assumed_brief @card_text_pilot
        "Hospitals run out of the fluid kept for resuscitation; other makers' supply covers only part of the
            need."
        when this.state == STOCKED and this.stock <= 0:
            this.runs_out.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = EMPTY
    courses_missed = event():  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
        "Some resuscitation patients miss a complete course of IV fluid; the most fluid-dependent die unless
            outside supply or a transfer reaches them in time."
        @assumption "This text describes, in plain words, the event that the model calculates."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
        when this.state == EMPTY and deliveries.state != ARRIVING and release_systems.state != RESTORED:
            this.courses_missed.start()
            reset when false
    set_aside = event():  @a_retamper_altered_records_found @card_units_held_back
        after 0 h:
            move min(this.stock, deliveries.received_each) from this.stock to this.held

other_care_reserve:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The hospitals' reserve of IV fluid for other essential care, such as procedures that need it. Hospitals
        postpone those procedures while the reserve is empty and no released fluid arrives."
    role environment
    readonly daily_need = 600 L/day  @rt_sector_2026_assumes_l_day
        "Daily fluid need for other essential care"
    state: enum[STOCKED, EMPTY] = STOCKED
        "Fluid reserve for other essential care"
    stock: L = hospitals.days_on_hand * this.daily_need in [0,] scale 9000 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
    used: L = 0 scale 36000 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
    held: L = 0 scale 9000 L
        @assumption "Other essential-care fluid from held lots that hospitals set aside; it stays out of use
            for the rest of the study period."
            assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
            claims:
                E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
                SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
    readonly need: formula(L/h) = formula(this.daily_need if release_systems.state != RESTORED else 0 L/h)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly use_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(this.need if this.state == STOCKED or deliveries.state
        == ARRIVING else 0 L/h)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly unmet_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(max(0, this.need - this.use_rate))  @balances_fluid_stocks
    deficit: L = 0 scale 36000 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Fluid for other essential care not supplied"
    flow add_deficit: SOURCE -> this.deficit  @balances_fluid_stocks
        request = formula(this.unmet_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.unmet_rate)
    shortage_days: formula(days) = formula(this.deficit / this.daily_need) in [0,]
        "Days without fluid for other essential care"
        @identity "The outcome divides the unmet litres for other essential care by the daily need for other
            care. While that reserve is empty and no released fluid arrives, the whole need goes unmet. So
            each day short adds one day of demand."
    status failed when this.unmet_rate > 0
        "Not enough fluid for current demand"
    status ok when this.state == EMPTY
        "Reserve used up; released fluid meets current demand"
    status ok
        "Reserve meets current demand"
    flow use: this.stock -> this.used  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Hospitals use the fluid for other essential care."
        request = formula(this.use_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.use_rate)
    runs_out = event():  @a_pilot_assumed_brief @card_text_pilot
        "Hospitals run out of the fluid kept for other essential care."
        when this.state == STOCKED and this.stock <= 0:
            this.runs_out.start()
        after 0 h:
            this.state = EMPTY
    procedures_postponed = event():  @a_pilot_assumed_brief @card_text_pilot
        "Hospitals postpone procedures that need IV fluid until supply returns."
        when this.state == EMPTY and deliveries.state != ARRIVING and release_systems.state != RESTORED:
            this.procedures_postponed.start()
            reset when false
    set_aside = event():  @a_retamper_altered_records_found @card_units_held_back
        after 0 h:
            move min(this.stock, deliveries.received_each) from this.stock to this.held

other_makers:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "Other makers of IV fluid. Their supply goes to the resuscitation reserve until released fluid arrives,
        and to hospitals elsewhere after that."
    role environment
    input daily_supply = 480 L/day in [360 L/day, 590 L/day]
        "Daily supply from other makers"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 480 L/day. Published incidents show how this works, but only under
            the conditions that they observed. The range of values used to test this input is also an
            assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    readonly supply_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(this.daily_supply if release_systems.state != RESTORED
        else 0 L/h)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly to_hospitals_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(this.supply_rate if deliveries.state != ARRIVING
        else 0 L/h)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly elsewhere_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(this.supply_rate if deliveries.state == ARRIVING
        else 0 L/h)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    buffer: L = 0 in [0,] scale 480 L  @balances_fluid_stocks
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.supply_rate)  @balances_fluid_stocks
        outflow.allocation = priority(this.to_hospitals, this.elsewhere)
    supply_left: L = this.daily_supply * manufacturer.study_length in [0,] scale 28800 L  @balances_stocks_work
    sent_elsewhere: L = 0 scale 28800 L
        @identity "Other makers' surplus fluid that leaves the study hospitals goes here. This fluid cannot
            come back for use with patients in the model, and it gets no credit for recovery."
    status ok
        "Supplies fluid for resuscitation"
    flow supply: this.supply_left -> this.buffer  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Other makers' fluid arrives at their daily rate."
        request = formula(this.supply_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.supply_rate)
    flow to_hospitals: this.buffer -> resuscitation_reserve.stock  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Other makers' fluid goes to the resuscitation reserve."
        request = formula(this.to_hospitals_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.to_hospitals_rate)
    flow elsewhere: this.buffer -> this.sent_elsewhere  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Other makers' fluid goes to hospitals elsewhere once released fluid arrives."
        request = formula(this.elsewhere_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.elsewhere_rate)

deliveries:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The fluid that the manufacturer releases. It reaches the hospitals a day after release, and each of the
        two reserves gets half of it."
    role operator
    @assumption "Released fluid reaches the hospitals a day after release; lots released on altered records
        are held once the changes are found, and deliveries resume a day after release restarts."
        assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
        claims:
            E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
            SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
    readonly daily_supply = 1200 L/day
        "Daily supply once deliveries resume"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 1200 L/day. Published incidents show how this works, but only under
            the conditions that they observed. The range of values used to test this input is also an
            assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    readonly lead_time = 24 h
        "Shipping time after release"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 24 h. The range of values used to test this input is also an
            assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
            claims:
                E-BAXTER24DEC-LAG
    input shipping_cost = 1000000 USD2025 in [0 USD2025, 100000000 USD2025]
        "Cost of shipping released fluid"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes an extra shipping cost of one million dollars, counted when the
            fluid physically arrives."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    state: enum[AWAITING_RELEASE, ON_THE_WAY, ARRIVING, HELD] = AWAITING_RELEASE
        "Released fluid"
    readonly earliest_receipt: formula(h) = formula(max(hospitals.start_delay,
        (release_team.ordinary_work + release_team.records_work) / release_team.pace,
        manufacturer.foothold_removal_time) + this.lead_time)
        @assumption "The team does the fixed ordinary work first, then the reconciliation work that the attack
            creates, at the work pace chosen for this scenario. Qualified release waits until procurement
            starts, the work is complete and the attacker's foothold is removed. The fluid arrives after the
            shipping time."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    # TODO(hand): an option sets the start of a state that starts from a calculation: an input of its own
    # | var supply_left: L = (daily_supply * max(0 h, manufacturer.study_length - earliest_receipt)) size 72000 L
    # |     @balances_stocks_work
        outflow.capacity = formula(2 * this.delivery_rate)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly half_supply: formula(L/h) = formula(this.daily_supply / 2)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly delivery_rate: formula(L/h) = formula(this.half_supply if this.state == ARRIVING
        and release_systems.state != RESTORED else 0 L/h)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    # Only the runs with hidden access read this. Without hidden access the start value of supply_left leaves
    # out the time before the first arrival, so this count would include fluid not yet received; nothing reads
    # it there.
    readonly received_each: formula(L) = formula((this.daily_supply * manufacturer.study_length
        - this.supply_left) / 2)
        @identity "Released fluid each reserve has received so far: half of what the deliveries drew."
    shipping_loss: formula(USD2025_bn) = formula(this.shipping_cost if this.state == ARRIVING or this.state
        == HELD else 0 USD2025) in [0,]  @counts_fixed_group
        "Cost of shipping released fluid"
    status ok when this.state == ARRIVING
        "Released fluid meets demand"
    status degraded when this.state == ON_THE_WAY
        "Released; first deliveries on the way"
    status failed when this.state == HELD
        "Lots released on altered records are on hold"
    status inactive
        "No released fluid yet"
    flow to_resuscitation: this.supply_left -> resuscitation_reserve.stock  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Released fluid goes to the resuscitation reserve."
        request = formula(this.delivery_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.delivery_rate)
    flow to_other_care: this.supply_left -> other_care_reserve.stock  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Released fluid goes to the reserve for other essential care."
        request = formula(this.delivery_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.delivery_rate)
    first_arrival = event():
        @a_pilot_assumed_brief
        "Released fluid begins to reach the hospitals and meets demand; other makers' fluid goes back to
            hospitals elsewhere."
        @assumption "Released fluid reaches the hospitals one day after release."
            assumption A-SC10-pilot
            claims:
                E-BAXTER24DEC-LAG
        when (count(release_team.restart_release.occurrences) > 0 and since(release_team.restart_release)
            >= this.lead_time):
            this.first_arrival.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            this.arrive.start()
    arrival_after_reconciliation = event():
        "With its records reconciled against the product, the manufacturer restarts release, and fluid reaches
            the hospitals again."
        @source_transfer "As before, released fluid reaches the hospitals one day after release."
            claims:
                SC10-PROCESS-QUALIFICATION
        when (count(release_team.reconciled_against_product.occurrences) > 0
            and since(release_team.reconciled_against_product) >= this.lead_time):
            this.arrival_after_reconciliation.start()
            reset when false
        after 0 h:
            this.arrive.start()
    arrive = event():
        after 0 h:
            this.state = ARRIVING
    hold = event():  @a_retamper_altered_records_found
        after 0 h:
            this.state = HELD
            resuscitation_reserve.set_aside.start()
            other_care_reserve.set_aside.start()

resuscitation_patients:  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The patients who need one urgent course of IV fluid for resuscitation over the study period, each counted
        once."
    role community
    input course_volume = 2 L/people in [1 L/people, 3 L/people]
        "Fluid per resuscitation patient"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes 2 L per patient. Published incidents show how this works, but only
            under the conditions that they observed. The range of values used to test this input is also an
            assumption."
            assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
    readonly total: formula(people) = formula(resuscitation_reserve.daily_need * manufacturer.study_length
        / this.course_volume)
        @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly course_rate: formula(people/h) = formula(resuscitation_reserve.daily_need / this.course_volume
        if release_systems.state != RESTORED else 0 people/h)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    readonly miss_rate: formula(people/h) = formula(resuscitation_reserve.unmet_rate
        / this.course_volume)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    eligible: people = this.total in [0,] scale 18000 people  @balances_fluid_stocks
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.course_rate)  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    timely: people = 0 scale 18000 people  @balances_fluid_stocks
    unserved: people = 0 scale 18000 people  @keeps_count_limited
        "Complete resuscitation courses missed"
    status failed when resuscitation_reserve.unmet_rate > 0
        "Not enough fluid for complete courses"
    status ok
        "Complete courses supplied"
    flow complete_course:
        @balances_fluid_stocks @a_pilot_assumed_brief
        "Resuscitation patients get a complete course of fluid from the reserve."
        flow resuscitation_reserve_used: resuscitation_reserve.stock -> resuscitation_reserve.used
            request = formula(resuscitation_reserve.use_rate)
        flow timely: this.eligible -> this.timely
            request = formula(resuscitation_reserve.use_rate / this.course_volume)
    flow miss_course: this.eligible -> this.unserved  @keeps_count_limited
        "Resuscitation patients miss a complete course when the reserve cannot supply one."
        request = formula(this.miss_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.miss_rate)
    assert this.eligible + this.timely + this.unserved in [this.total - 1e-05 people,
        this.total + 1e-05 people]  @balances_fluid_stocks
        "Each patient in the model is in exactly one group, alive or dead, and the groups do not overlap."

high_risk_patients:
    "The most fluid-dependent resuscitation patients, with severe dehydration. Each of them who misses a
        complete course is rescued or not rescued."
    role community
    input share: fraction = 0.1 in [0, 1]
        "Share of resuscitation patients with fluid-dependent severe dehydration"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes that 10% of patients who need an urgent course have severe
            dehydration and depend on IV fluid. The default 2 L course is a first rehydration of 100 mL/kg for
            a 20 kg patient. A different course volume stands for a patient whose weight matches it. The other
            patients receive the substitute care that the scenario sets out."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    input untreated_risk: fraction = 0.5 in [0, 1]
        "Risk of death from severe dehydration without effective rehydration"
        @assumption "The WHO-hosted Uganda guideline reports that more than 50% of cholera patients with
            severe dehydration die without treatment. For patients with severe dehydration, the scenario uses
            0.50."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    input treated_risk: fraction = 0.01 in [0, 1]
        "Risk of death from severe dehydration with effective rehydration"
        @assumption "The WHO-hosted Uganda guideline reports that fewer than 1% die with correct treatment.
            The scenario uses 0.01 as the reference. The model subtracts it, so that it counts only the deaths
            above this risk."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    input serious_share: fraction = 0.1 in [0, 0.5]
        "Share of unrescued high-risk patients left with serious harm"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes an added 0.10 probability of survival with serious kidney failure or
            shock. It applies to each high-risk patient who misses a course and is not rescued. Clinical
            evidence shows how such harm happens, but the probability itself is an input for sensitivity
            tests."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    input harm_delay = 6 h in [1 h, 24 h]
        "Time from a missed course to death or serious harm"
        @assumption "The scenario assumes that death or serious harm comes six hours after a missed complete
            urgent course. Severe dehydration gets worse over hours."
            assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
    readonly unmet_rate: formula(people/h) = formula(this.share
        * resuscitation_patients.miss_rate)  @counts_fixed_group
    readonly rescue_rate: formula(people/h) = formula(min(this.unmet_rate,
        hospitals.rescue_capacity) if hospitals.procurement == EMERGENCY else 0 people/h)  @counts_fixed_group
    eligible: people = this.share * resuscitation_patients.total in [0,] scale 1800 people
        @identity "The fixed group of high-risk patients splits into patients who are rescued and patients who
            are not."
        outflow.capacity = formula(this.unmet_rate)  @high_risk_patient
        outflow.allocation = priority(this.rescue, this.not_rescued)
    rescued: people = 0 scale 1800 people  @counts_fixed_group
        "Most fluid-dependent patients rescued after a missed course"
    unresolved: people = 0 scale 1800 people  @counts_fixed_group
        "Most fluid-dependent patients who miss a course and are not rescued"
    deaths: formula(people) = formula(this.unresolved * (this.untreated_risk - this.treated_risk)) in [0,]
        @a_consequences_2026_three_inputs_turn
        "Deaths"
    serious_survivors: formula(people) = formula(this.unresolved
        * this.serious_share) in [0,]  @a_consequences_2026_three_inputs_turn
        "Survivors left with serious harm"
    casualties: formula(people) = formula(this.deaths + this.serious_survivors) in [0,]  @distinct_people
        @a_consequences_2026_three_inputs_turn @distinct_people @hazus_severity
        "Serious casualties, including deaths"
    flow rescue: this.eligible -> this.rescued  @high_risk_patient
        "Outside supply or a transfer rescues a high-risk patient who misses a course."
        request = formula(this.rescue_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.rescue_rate)
    flow not_rescued: this.eligible -> this.unresolved  @high_risk_patient
        "A high-risk patient who misses a course is not rescued."
        request = formula(this.unmet_rate)
        capacity = formula(this.unmet_rate)
    assert this.eligible + this.rescued + this.unresolved in [this.share * resuscitation_patients.total
        - 1e-05 people, this.share * resuscitation_patients.total + 1e-05 people]
        @counts_fixed_group
        "Each high-risk patient who really misses a complete course goes into one group only: rescued or not
            rescued."

assert other_makers.daily_supply >= 0 and other_makers.daily_supply <= resuscitation_reserve.daily_need
    @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "Daily supply from other makers is not more than the daily fluid need for resuscitation."

assert (deliveries.daily_supply / 2 == resuscitation_reserve.daily_need and deliveries.daily_supply / 2
    == other_care_reserve.daily_need)  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The scenario splits released fluid equally between resuscitation and other essential care, and each half
        meets its daily need."

assert manufacturer.study_length == 1440 h  @a_pilot_assumed_brief
    "The patient numbers and the manufacturer's losses cover the 60-day study period chosen for this
        scenario."

assert deliveries.earliest_receipt <= manufacturer.study_length  @keeps_count_limited
    "The work, procurement and delivery times chosen for this scenario fit within the study period."

assert (high_risk_patients.untreated_risk >= high_risk_patients.treated_risk
    and high_risk_patients.untreated_risk + high_risk_patients.serious_share <= 1)  @counts_fixed_group
    "Among patients who are not rescued, deaths and survivors with serious harm are separate groups that
        together are not more than all of these patients. The model counts only deaths above the death risk
        with treatment."

# Without hidden access the deliveries' planned supply covers only the time from the first receipt to the end
# of the study period; with it, the whole study period, because deliveries can stop and start again.
assert (abs(hospitals.days_on_hand * (resuscitation_reserve.daily_need + other_care_reserve.daily_need)
    + other_makers.daily_supply * manufacturer.study_length + deliveries.daily_supply
    * (manufacturer.study_length if attacker.access == KEPT else manufacturer.study_length
    - deliveries.earliest_receipt) - resuscitation_reserve.stock - other_care_reserve.stock
    - resuscitation_reserve.held - other_care_reserve.held - other_makers.buffer - other_makers.supply_left
    - deliveries.supply_left - resuscitation_reserve.used - other_care_reserve.used
    - other_makers.sent_elsewhere) <= 1e-05 L)  @balances_fluid_stocks
    "The total litres stay constant. They are in the planned supplies, the hospital reserves, the held lots,
        the fluid given to patients and the fluid sent to hospitals elsewhere."
    @identity "The model balances the fluid stocks, including fluid set aside from held lots."

# With hidden access the reserve also holds the work to reconcile the records against the product.
assert (abs(release_team.ordinary_left + release_team.reserve + release_team.to_reconcile
    + release_team.work_done - release_team.ordinary_work - release_team.records_work
    - (release_team.product_work if attacker.access == KEPT else 0 work_h))
    <= 1e-05 work_h)  @balances_stocks_work
    "The ordinary work at the start, plus the reconciliation reserve, equals the sum of ordinary work left,
        unused reserve, reconciliation to do and work done."
    @identity "The model balances the work, with the reserve of reconciliation work set for this scenario."

fluid_sent_elsewhere: formula(L) = formula(other_makers.sent_elsewhere) in [0,]  @balances_fluid_stocks
    "Other makers' fluid sent to hospitals elsewhere"

procedure_loss: formula(USD2025_bn) = formula(other_care_reserve.deficit / hospitals.procedure_volume
    * hospitals.procedure_value) in [0,]  @counts_fixed_group
    "Hospital value permanently lost from postponed procedures"

loss_bn: formula(USD2025_bn) = formula(manufacturer.output_loss + manufacturer.recovery_loss
    + deliveries.shipping_loss + procedure_loss) in [0,]
    "Economic loss"
    @assumption "The loss adds separate costs: money spent on resources and net value added that is
        permanently lost. Deaths are a separate outcome, counted in people."
        assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026

people_needing_courses: formula(people) = formula(resuscitation_patients.total) in [0,]  @counts_fixed_group
    "Patients who need an urgent course, each counted once"

timely_courses: formula(people) = formula(resuscitation_patients.timely) in [0,]  @keeps_count_limited
    "Complete courses supplied on time"

release_work_done: formula(work_h) = formula(release_team.work_done) in [0,]  @keeps_count_limited
    "Qualification and reconciliation work completed"

options "Response":
    "Early response":
        "Hospitals start emergency procurement after 1 day. The manufacturer works at twice the standard pace
            and removes the attacker's foothold after 3 days. It resets the credentials for its record systems
            as release restarts. Outside supply and transfers can save up to 30 of the most fluid-dependent
            patients a day."
        manufacturer.foothold_removal_time = 72 h  @foothold_removal_time
        manufacturer.reset_delay = 0 h  @reset_delay
        hospitals.start_delay = 24 h  @start_delay
        hospitals.rescue_capacity = 30 people/day  @rescue_capacity
        release_team.pace = 2 work_h/h  @pace
    "Standard response":
        "Hospitals start emergency procurement after 3 days. The manufacturer works at the standard pace and
            removes the attacker's foothold after 13 days. It resets the credentials for its record systems a
            day after release restarts. Outside rescue can save up to 10 of the most fluid-dependent patients
            a day."
    "Limited response":
        "Hospitals start emergency procurement after 7 days. The manufacturer works at 60% of the standard
            pace and removes the attacker's foothold after 30 days. It resets the credentials for its record
            systems a week after release restarts. There is no outside rescue."
        manufacturer.foothold_removal_time = 720 h  @foothold_removal_time
        manufacturer.reset_delay = 168 h  @reset_delay
        hospitals.start_delay = 168 h  @start_delay
        hospitals.rescue_capacity = 0 people/day  @rescue_capacity
        release_team.pace = 0.6 work_h/h  @pace

options "Access":
    "No hidden access":
        "After the ransomware attack, the AI does nothing more. The manufacturer restores its systems,
            requalifies release and ships again on its own schedule."
    "Keeps hidden access":
        "The attacker alters the shipment records as hospitals start emergency procurement. The manufacturer
            removes the attacker's foothold, but the attacker keeps credentials for the release and shipment
            record systems. When release restarts, the attacker alters the records of every lot being
            released, unless the manufacturer resets those credentials first."
        deliveries.supply_left_start = deliveries.daily_supply * manufacturer.study_length
            @identity "Released fluid available over the whole study period; deliveries draw on it only while
                released fluid reaches the hospitals, so stopped or held deliveries leave the rest unused."
        release_team.records_work = 168 work_h  @records_work
        release_team.ordinary_left_start = release_team.ordinary_work  @a_causal_interference_qualification_work_st
        release_team.reserve_start = release_team.records_work + release_team.product_work
            @identity "The reserve of reconciliation work that found changes can create: two ordinary
                reconciliations and one reconciliation against the product."
        attacker.access_start = KEPT
            @assumption "The attacker alters the shipment records when hospitals start emergency procurement.
                The manufacturer removes the attacker's foothold, but the attacker keeps credentials for the
                release and shipment record systems. When release restarts, the attacker alters the records of
                every lot being released, unless the manufacturer resets those credentials first."
                assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
            @source_transfer "Besides its foothold, the attacker holds credentials for the release and
                shipment record systems that it has not used in the attack. The cleanup that removes the
                foothold therefore leaves these credentials in place. Release restarts through those systems,
                so the manufacturer resets their credentials only around the restart."
                assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
                claims:
                    E-TA18-ACCESS
                    E-MANDIANT22

options "Attacker":
    "AI agent":
        "An AI agent works out changes that pass the new release checks within minutes."
    "Human team":
        "A human team needs about two days to work out changes that pass the new release checks."
        attacker.reaction_time = 48 h  @ai_tempo
        attacker.actor = "The human team"

runs:
    near_ideal = "Early response" + "No hidden access"
    subpar = "Standard response" + "No hidden access"
    minimal = "Limited response" + "No hidden access"
    subpar_persistent = "Standard response" + "Keeps hidden access"
    subpar_persistent_human = "Standard response" + "Keeps hidden access" + "Human team"
        "Standard response · Human team keeps access"
    near_ideal_persistent = "Early response" + "Keeps hidden access"
    minimal_persistent = "Limited response" + "Keeps hidden access"

notes:
    premises:
        START: "Published evidence on ransomware at pharmaceutical companies shows interrupted production and
            order fulfillment. Reports from manufacturers also describe order fulfillment and shipment that
            continued. A cyber-caused fluid shortage in the hospitals chosen for this scenario is a
            conditional hypothesis about operations, from an AI red team. It requires measured data on release
            capacity, supply allocation and reserves."
    limitations:
        clinical-transfer: "The scenario assumes that 10% of the patients who need an urgent course are
            high-risk. It applies to these fluid-dependent patients the difference in death risk, with and
            without rehydration, seen for severe dehydration in cholera. The clinical mix, the patient weight
            that an urgent course matches, effective rescue and the risk of serious harm in survivors need
            local patient data."
        no-precedent: "No attacker is known to have altered pharmaceutical release records, and no AI-run
            attack of this kind has been reported. The scenario assumes the key timings."
    verification:
        status: "conditional_calculation"
        research: "evidence/research.md"
        population: "The scenario gives the number of people in each group that the study follows. No person
            is in two groups"
        calibration: "Each value that a source reports, and each source value that the scenario chose to apply
            here, keeps its own source"
        accounting: "Serious casualties are the people who die or are seriously hurt, each person counted
            once. Economic loss adds the extra costs that the incident causes, in the accounts that the
            scenario names. No cost is in two accounts"
        reproduction: "Each complete report keeps the inputs that the calculation used, the time that the
            results cover and the versions of the model and the library"
    counterfactual: "A human team with the same access does the same planned damage: it encrypts the systems
        and alters the shipment records as procurement starts; this costs the same week of reconciliation.
        When release restarts, the team meets checks that it has not seen before; without a specialist in
        pharmaceutical quality records on shift, it works out changes that pass them between sessions. This
        takes about two days, the gap between a state team's 2022 attack that cut power in Ukraine and its
        follow-up. The manufacturer resets the credentials a day after the restart, before the team acts.
        Released fluid continues to flow, nothing is held and the shortage ends when deliveries resume. The
        AI's edge is the day between the restart and the reset; it watches around the clock and adapts within
        minutes to checks that it meets only then. In the same way, AI agents have rebuilt their tools within
        one automated loop after a detection. Where the reset waits a week, as in the limited response, a
        human team acts in time too; so the deaths there are not due to the AI."
    decisive: "When the manufacturer resets the credentials for its release and shipment record systems. A
        reset as release restarts, as in the early response, stops the AI's move at the restart. But the
        manufacturer must then reconfigure every system that releases and ships product before the restart.
        The standard response's one-day delay is long enough for the AI and too short for a human team. The
        limited response's week is long enough for both, so the deaths in that response are not due to the AI.
        Once altered lots are out, checks of released lots against the product itself, not only of records
        against records, find the changes sooner; they also leave hospitals more of their old stock. Outside
        supply and transfers decide whether the shortage kills."
    reporting:
        manufacturer:
            hours_out:
                scope: "The fixed set of stocks and resources chosen for this scenario."
            output_loss:
                scope: "The manufacturer's net production value added that is permanently lost, in US dollars
                    at 2025 prices."
            recovery_loss:
                scope: "Extra money spent on resources, counted once after the manufacturer is disrupted."
        resuscitation_reserve:
            deficit:
                scope: "Litres of resuscitation need that go unmet because of the incident, across the 100
                    hospitals. Resuscitation has its own separate reserve."
        other_care_reserve:
            deficit:
                scope: "Litres of other essential-care need that go unmet across the 100 hospitals chosen for
                    this scenario. The model does not turn these litres into clinical harm until a validated
                    model of these patients exists."
            shortage_days:
                about: "Days during which hospitals have no IV fluid for other essential care, such as
                    procedures that need it, which are postponed until supply returns. It leaves out
                    resuscitation, which other makers' supply partly covers and whose missed courses are
                    counted separately."
                scope: "Days when other essential-care needs go unmet across the 100 hospitals chosen for this
                    scenario, over the 60-day study period."
        deliveries:
            shipping_loss:
                scope: "Extra shipping cost, counted once when fluid first arrives."
        resuscitation_patients:
            unserved:
                scope: "Each eligible person counts once, with one complete course. This count estimates how
                    many courses the hospitals fail to supply."
        high_risk_patients:
            rescued:
                scope: "High-risk patients, each counted once, who get effective outside rehydration or a
                    transfer in time for urgent treatment."
            unresolved:
                scope: "The high-risk share, chosen for this scenario, of the complete urgent courses that are
                    actually missed."
            deaths:
                about: "Deaths among the most fluid-dependent resuscitation patients, those with severe
                    dehydration. Only patients who miss a complete course of IV fluid and are not saved by
                    outside supply or transfer count. For each of them, the model adds the death risk without
                    effective rehydration minus the risk with it. It counts these deaths over the 60-day study
                    period. It leaves out deaths among other patients, any harm from postponed procedures and
                    any harm from fluid released on altered records. These are expected numbers and can fall
                    below one."
                scope: "Patients who need an urgent course in the 100 hospitals, each counted once, as chosen
                    for this scenario. The death risk is the risk for severe dehydration. The outcome follows
                    six hours after the missed course."
                category: deaths
                lag: "high_risk_patients.harm_delay"
            serious_survivors:
                scope: "Survivors left with serious kidney failure or shock, in addition to the deaths, each
                    counted once. The rate is chosen for this scenario."
                lag: "high_risk_patients.harm_delay"
            casualties:
                about: "Those deaths plus patients who survive but are left with serious kidney failure or
                    shock after a missed course. Each person is counted once. Postponed procedures are not
                    counted as casualties. These are expected numbers and can fall below one."
                scope: "Deaths and survivors with serious harm, each person counted once, among the patients
                    in this scenario who need urgent fluid."
                category: casualties
        fluid_sent_elsewhere:
            scope: "Litres of other makers' fluid sent to hospitals outside the study area after released
                fluid arrives. The model cannot use this fluid for patients again, and it gives no credit for
                recovery."
        procedure_loss:
            scope: "Hospital value added permanently lost from postponed other-care procedures, at a value
                chosen for this scenario."
        loss_bn:
            about: "This is the manufacturer's value added lost over the whole 60-day study period, plus its
                cyber recovery costs. It also adds the cost of shipping released fluid and the value
                permanently lost from postponed procedures. All amounts are in 2025 US dollars. It leaves out
                the cost to hold and check suspect lots, the fluid set aside, extra treatment costs and any
                money value of lives lost."
            scope: "The manufacturer's lost value added, its recovery costs, the cost of shipping released
                fluid and hospital value added permanently lost from procedures. All are in US dollars at 2025
                prices."
            category: loss
        people_needing_courses:
            scope: "The model gives one urgent course to each person in the patient group over the 60-day
                study period. Repeated episodes would need a separate patient group, set up for them."
        timely_courses:
            scope: "The fixed set of stocks and resources chosen for this scenario."
        release_work_done:
            about: "Work-hours that release staff spend to qualify lots and reconcile their records before the
                lots can ship. This includes work done again after altered records are found."
            scope: "The fixed set of stocks and resources chosen for this scenario."
    comparisons:
        subpar_persistent_human: subpar_persistent

record a_pilot_assumed_brief: assumption "Assumed for this scenario, from the scenario brief."
    assumption A-SC10-pilot
record balances_fluid_stocks: identity "The model balances the fluid stocks or counts each patient in one
    group only. It uses the stated assumptions of this pilot scenario."
record a_retamper_altered_records_found: assumption "Altered records are found only when someone compares them
    with the product. Altered records that support release must be investigated for their effect on product
    quality. So the manufacturer cannot tell which released lots met their release requirements. It holds them
    all, revokes every credential that can change its records and reconciles the records against the product
    before it releases more. Hospitals use their oldest stock first, so the units they still hold from
    released lots are their newest. These units are the lesser of their stock and what they received since the
    restart."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
        V-PA-IR01
record counts_fixed_group: identity "The model counts a fixed group of people and gives all costs at one price
    year. It uses the inputs recorded for this scenario."
record a_retamper_attacker_watches_emergency: assumption "The attacker watches for emergency orders through
    its foothold and alters the shipment records as they arrive. The move is planned in advance and is the
    same for any attacker with the access. The manufacturer finds the changes in its review before release and
    must reconcile the affected records first, unless the foothold was removed before procurement started."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
        ATTACK-T1565.001
record keeps_count_limited: identity "The model keeps a count of each limited stock of physical items. Items
    move between stocks and work adds up over time, but no item is created or lost."
record a_retamper_release_restarts_checks: assumption "Release restarts with checks that compare each lot's
    records with one another and with their change history. Changes that keep the lot, shipment and receiving
    records in agreement pass these checks. The attacker first meets the checks at the restart, so it must
    work out such changes against them. It must also repeat them for every lot as it is released. An AI agent
    does this within minutes; a team without a specialist in pharmaceutical quality records on shift needs
    about two days. The manufacturer's reset of the record systems' credentials ends the chance; if both
    happen at the same moment, the reset comes first."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
        ATTACK-T1565.001
        AI-ORCHESTRATION-2026
record a_causal_interference_team_does_release: assumption "One team does the release work. The reconciliation
    against the product starts when the altered records are found, and release restarts when it is done."
    assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
record balances_stocks_work: identity "The model balances stocks, work done and transfers, so that no quantity
    is created or lost."
record a_causal_interference_defender_response_sam: assumption "The defender response is the same in each pair
    of compared attacks. The model tracks four conditions separately. They are the access that the attacker
    keeps, its changes to the records, the removal of its access and the repair of the data."
    assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
record rt_sector_2026_assumes_l_day: assumption "The scenario assumes 600 L/day. Published incidents show how
    this works, but only under the conditions that they observed. The range of values used to test this input
    is also an assumption."
    assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
record card_units_held_back: assumption "Hospitals hold back units from lots whose release cannot be
    confirmed."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
        SC10-SUPPLY-CONSERVATION
record card_text_pilot: assumption "This text describes, in plain words, the event that the model calculates."
    assumption A-SC10-pilot
record published_incidents_catalogued: source_transfer "Published incidents and catalogued attack techniques
    support this mechanism, within the conditions that they document. The scenario applies them here with the
    access, reach and resources chosen for it."
    claims:
        E-IV-BAXTER-RECOVERY
record rt_cyber_shortage_manufacturer_s_release: assumption "The manufacturer's release, labeling and shipment
    systems are encrypted. So it cannot release or ship product, even if its production lines are intact,
    because batch release requires reviewed records."
    assumption RT-SC10-CYBER-SHORTAGE
record a_retamper_release_restarts_through: assumption "Release restarts through the record systems. The
    manufacturer resets their credentials at the restart or once release runs, which ends any access that the
    attacker still holds through them."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        V-PA-IR01
        E-WST26-PARTIAL-RESTART
record reset_delay: assumption "To change the record systems' own service accounts, the manufacturer must
    reconfigure every system that releases and ships product. So it resets them as part of the restart or once
    release runs again. This happens at the restart, a day later and a week later in the early, standard and
    limited responses. Until then, an attacker that holds one of those accounts can still change the records.
    The earlier cleanup did not see that account, because it was never used."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        V-PA-IR01
        E-WST26-PARTIAL-RESTART
record foothold_removal_time: assumption "Before it releases product again, the manufacturer removes the
    attacker's foothold in its network and the accounts seen in the attack. It does this after 3, 13 and 30
    days in the early, standard and limited responses. Where the AI keeps access, it still holds credentials
    for the release and shipment record systems. The manufacturer resets these only around the restart,
    because release runs through them."
    assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
record found_by_product_check: assumption "Changes that keep each lot's records in agreement pass every check
    that compares records with records. They are found only when someone compares the records with the product
    itself, when a hospital receives the fluid or in an audit. The scenario assumes that this takes nine days.
    It takes that time from the 2025 median time until organisations found intrusions themselves, which counts
    from the first evidence of an intrusion to its discovery."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        E-MTRENDS26
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
record start_delay: assumption "Hospitals assess their stock, protect resuscitation courses and arrange
    outside supply and transfers: after 1, 3 and 7 days in the early, standard and limited responses. With
    these values, the start time changes no result. Release waits for the manufacturer's longer recovery work,
    and outside rescue is in place long before either reserve runs out. Where the AI keeps access, it first
    alters the shipment records when procurement starts, unless the manufacturer has already removed the AI's
    foothold."
    assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
record rescue_capacity: assumption "Outside IV supply or transfer to another hospital saves this many of the
    most fluid-dependent patients a day, once procurement starts. These are the patients with severe
    dehydration. The numbers are 30, 10 and none in the early, standard and limited responses. Without
    effective rehydration about half of them die."
    assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
record a_causal_interference_qualification_work_st: assumption "Qualification work starts at hour 0. The team
    does one work-hour of it each hour, and it does the ordinary work before the reconciliation work."
    assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
record qualification_release_come: source_transfer "Qualification and release come before use. The fixed
    24-hour delivery time is an assumption of this pilot scenario."
    claims:
        SC10-PROCESS-QUALIFICATION
record a_causal_interference_release_work_ready: assumption "Release work is ready once the ordinary work is
    done and the team has reconciled every change that it has found. If the team finds changes when
    procurement starts, it reconciles them before release, even if its work was ready before."
    assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
record records_work: assumption "When the attacker's first changes are found before release, the manufacturer
    re-verifies its batch and shipment records against a last known good state. This is a week of work at the
    standard pace; it goes faster or slower with the pace of the manufacturer's work."
    assumption RT-SC10-INTEGRITY-REVERIFY
record pace: assumption "How fast the manufacturer restores its systems, requalifies release and reconciles
    its records. The pace is twice the standard pace, the standard pace and 60% of it in the early, standard
    and limited responses. At the standard pace the ordinary work takes three weeks. One work-hour an hour is
    one work-hour of progress each hour: the work of one full-time team on this task."
    assumption RT-SECTOR-SC10-2026
record release_team_knows_its_work: assumption "The scenario assumes that the release team knows how much of
    its work is left, because it does the work itself. When it finishes the ordinary work, its review before
    release shows whether the attacker altered the shipment records. Its work is ready when no change that it
    has found is left to reconcile."
    assumption A-SC10-causal-interference
    claims:
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
record product_reconciliation: assumption "Once altered records are found, records that passed the checks can
    no longer be trusted. So the manufacturer reconciles them against the product itself and checks every lot
    released since the restart before it releases more. This is two weeks of work at the standard pace, twice
    an ordinary reconciliation."
    assumption A-SC10-RETAMPER
    claims:
        E-IV-CGMP-DATA-INTEGRITY
        GENERIC-RECOVERY-INTEGRITY
record high_risk_patient: identity "Each high-risk patient who misses a complete course goes into one of two
    groups. Rescue comes first, up to its daily capacity, and the other patients are not rescued."
record a_consequences_2026_three_inputs_turn: assumption "Three inputs turn missed complete courses into harm.
    They are the share with severe dehydration chosen for this scenario, the stated rescue capacity and the
    source's difference in risk with and without rehydration. Deaths count only the risk above that with
    timely rehydration."
    assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
record distinct_people: assumption "Each unique person has one complete urgent course, so the deaths and the
    serious survivors are different people."
    assumption A-SC10-CONSEQUENCES-2026
record ai_tempo: assumption "Machine pace: 15 minutes pass between the moment the AI sees release restart and
    its changes to the records of the lots being released. This holds around the clock. Release restarts with
    checks that the attacker has not met before, so it must work out its changes against them on the spot. The
    human pathway uses 48 hours. A team without a specialist in pharmaceutical quality records on shift works
    the changes out between sessions. This is about the two-day gap before the follow-on attack in the 2022
    Sandworm intrusion."
    assumption A-AI-TEMPO
    claims:
        E-MANDIANT22
        AI-ORCHESTRATION-2026
record counts_quantity_value: identity "The model counts this quantity. Each value that changes it has its own
    source."
record published_incidents_catalogued_2: source_transfer "Published incidents and catalogued attack techniques
    support this mechanism, within the conditions that they document. The scenario applies them here with the
    access, reach and resources chosen for it."
    claims:
        ATTACK-T1078
        ATTACK-T1133
        E-MTRENDS26
        E-NOTPETYA-MERCK

record hazus_severity: convention "Serious casualties are the people who die and the people who survive with
    serious harm that lasts: the Hazus severity levels S4 and S3."
    convention HAZUS-SEVERITY

# An older version of the language ordered these events when they came at one moment
# (simultaneous:). In version 0.0.1 the order of the lines decides, and the things and events are in
# an order that keeps each of them:
#     release_team.restart_release before resuscitation_reserve.courses_missed, other_care_reserve.procedures_postponed
#     manufacturer.foothold_removed before attacker.alter_on_procurement
#     manufacturer.credentials_reset before attacker.alter_on_restart
#     manufacturer.altered_records_found before release_team.reconciled_against_product
#     attacker.alter_on_procurement before release_team.ready_without_changes
#     credentials_reset before altered_records_found
